    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "LOCATION:\r\n\r\nThe property is located in a fantastic well laid out modern residential development within walking distance of Monivea village with Monivea Demesne woods close by offering local walkways and trails in a serene country village setting.\r\n\r\nMonivea is located approx. 5.5 miles from Athenry town and approximately 15 miles from Galway city and is a picturesque and very popular village with its unique wide open greens and steeped in strong local history. The Stables is located on a beautiful site with stone wall front boundary and is just a leisurely stroll to the village. All in all an excellent residential location with all the local residential amenities to hand to include new contemporary local National School, Shops, Church, Pubs, Garda barracks , Post Office , children’s playground and a wide range of local community facilities and entertainment facilities. Galway city is within an easy commute.  The area is also renowned for its sporting culture.\r\n\r\nDESCRIPTION:\r\n\r\nNumber 18 The Stables is a fantastic ready to walk into splendid 3/4 bedroom semi detached home situated towards the rear of this small estate overlooking the centre green in a lovely private and quaint setting within a short stroll of the picturesque village.  The property is beautifully presented and boasts many excellent modern features combining excellent natural lighting with generously proportioned accommodation with a A3 BER rating.  The heart of the house is the superbly laid out kitchen with lovely centre island unit, fully fitted kitchen with patio doors out to the South West facing rear garden and French doors linking into the front living room.  \r\n\r\nUpstairs the property has 3 fine bedrooms, however the house was a 4 bedroom house on the plans as the purchaser combined the second front bedroom as a walk in wardrobe area to the master en-suite bedroom.  This can easily be adapted back to a 4 bedroom should a purchaser require.  The first floor is beautifully presented with excellent natural lighting with lovely floors and impeccable pristine order.  Outside the property has spacious tarmac driveway with ample parking, nice front garden and enclosed rear lawned garden with patio area and small garden shed.  Other features include beautiful feature shutters to front windows, fitted alarm, oil fired central heating, solar panels, PVC double glazed windows and doors, solid fuel stove.  The property is constructed of concrete block construction and is excellently appointed.  \r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION:\r\n\r\nEntrance Hall\twith laminate floor, staircase with stairlift\r\nSitting Room\twith laminate floor, solid fuel stove, french doors to sitting room\r\nKitchen/dining room\twith fitted kitchen, oven & hob, centre island unit, fitted units, patio door, integrated microwave, larder, extractor hood, larder\r\nUtility\twith fitted units, plumbed for washing machine & drier, back door\r\nDownstairs toilet\twith wc, whb\r\n\r\nUpstairs:\r\nMaster Bedroom (front)\twith laminate floor, walk in wardrobe\r\n(Originally 2 bedrooms on the plans)\r\nNote: The second bedroom that is currently used as a walk in wardrobe for the master en-suite could easily be returned to an individual room by reinstating its own doorway onto the landing.  \r\nEnsuite\twith wc, whb, shower, fully tiled\r\n\r\nBedroom 2\tdouble at back, carpet\r\nLanding\twith carpet, hot press\r\nBedroom 3\tdouble, with carpet\r\nBathroom\twith wc, whb, shower, fully tiled\r\n\r\nOutside:\t\r\n\r\nFront tarmac driveway with ample parking\r\nEnclosed lawned rear garden\r\nSmall garden Shed\r\nSide access way\r\nOil Boiler encased\r\n\r\nSERVICES:\r\n\r\nWe understand the property has all mains services available to same.  There is a central treatment plant serving the development, the maintenance of which is covered under the management fee structure.  \r\n\r\n\r\nMANAGEMENT FEES:\r\n\r\nThere is a management company in place for this estate and the yearly fee is approximately €1,135 (2025 Figure).  \r\n\t \r\n\r\n\r\nGUIDE PRICE:\t€395,000\r\n\r\nVIEWINGS:\r\n\r\nViewings are strictly by appointment with Auctioneers who are sole selling Agents."
      },
